  "coverageFile": "./data/avalanche/avalanche-coverage-pilot.geojson",
  "limitations": [
    "Experimental terrain modeling. Not an avalanche hazard map, not an ATES rating, not a forecast; it says nothing about current snowpack, stability, or whether any slope is safe.",
    "Absence of modeled release or runout does not mean terrain is safe or free of avalanche exposure. Start zones smaller than about 20-30 m (cornices, gullies, cliff bands, convex rolls), avalanches larger than the alpha angle allows, and release outside the pilot can reach unshaded terrain.",
    "Parameters are published defaults: PRA from AutoATES v2.0 (two western Canada test areas), runout from the Flow-Py v1.0 regional example (Austria). None is calibrated or validated for Colorado.",
    "PRA is a fuzzy terrain-suitability membership from slope, wind shelter and canopy cover; it is not a release probability.",
    "Flow-Py solves no time-dependent equations. zDelta is an energy-line height (a geometric intensity proxy), not a speed, depth, pressure or arrival time; cell counts are numbers of modeled paths, not reach probabilities.",
    "Forest enters only the PRA (canopy cover). The runout ignores forest friction, so modeled runout into forest is likely too long. Canopy is 2025 NLCD Tree Canopy Cover at 30 m; standing dead trees and recent disturbance are poorly represented.",
    "Bare-earth 10 m DEM resampled from USGS 3DEP 1/3 arc-second; snow surface, cornices and small terrain features are not represented.",
    "Inside the truncation band near the pilot edge the runout is incomplete (paths from outside the pilot are missing and paths leaving it are cut)."
  ],
